    {
      "id": 116754,
      "name": "lutherbellhendricksv",
      "username": "lutherbellhendricksv",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/lutherbellhendricksv/{size}/2350_2.png",
      "created_at": "2014-09-03T20:31:05.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Donner\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/donner/48/1903_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Donner:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Actually, the wording says you can take the action again a third time for free. &nbsp;It doesn't say whether you can take another action between or not.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>The ability triggers when you use an ability for the second time in a turn. At that time, you may use it a third time for free, or you may choose not to. You can't use it a third time for free later in the turn; only right then.</p>",
